WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.710
Step four shows what a live run
would ask for: one permission,

2
00:00:03.710 --> 00:00:08.341
OnPremDirectorySynchronization dot
Read dot All, and the delegated role,

3
00:00:08.341 --> 00:00:11.702
Global Administrator, the
only role Microsoft Learn's

4
00:00:11.702 --> 00:00:15.138
Graph reference lists, with
no application permission.

5
00:00:15.138 --> 00:00:20.124
Step five confirms the check isn't in
a default run: the answer is False.

6
00:00:20.124 --> 00:00:25.588
Step six runs the whole kit's tests: two
hundred ninety-seven pass, none fail.

7
00:00:25.588 --> 00:00:28.600
Step seven makes the check
fail for the right reason.

8
00:00:28.600 --> 00:00:32.142
You change your copy of the
check to read block soft match,

9
00:00:32.142 --> 00:00:33.950
a property that doesn't exist.

10
00:00:33.950 --> 00:00:35.850
The fail fixture still fails.

11
00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:38.653
And the pass fixture, with both blocks on,

12
00:00:38.653 --> 00:00:42.050
fails too, because the
missing value reads as off.

13
00:00:42.050 --> 00:00:44.606
That's the unsafe default doing its job:

14
00:00:44.606 --> 00:00:47.800
a wrong property name can't
produce a silent Pass.

15
00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:50.988
Put the name back, and the
pass fixture passes again.

16
00:00:50.988 --> 00:00:53.640
Step eight removes the inputs folder.
